| History                 = '''Tony Stark''' was a billionaire playboy and industrialist who owned [[Stark Industries (Earth-8096)|Stark Industries]]. He supplied [[Strategic Homeland Intervention, Enforcement and Logistics Division (Earth-8096)|S.H.I.E.L.D.]] and the United States Military with advanced weapons and other necessities. However at some point Stark suffered an injury damaging his heart to keep alive, he embedded his invention the [[Arc Reactor]] in his chest to stay alive; the reactor which provided an adequate power source for his Iron Man armors he would later invent. Stark would later abandon his ambitions of providing weapons to the military and focus on peaceful usage of his inventions. 

===Working Solo===
Shortly before joining the [[Avengers (Earth-8096)|Avengers]], Tony Stark was seen in combat with a large robot. Not long after defeating the giant robot he was told about an attack on the [[United Nations Headquarters]]. With many people in danger including the president of the United States. Tony quickly donned the Iron Man armor and engaged the attackers; who at this point were identified as agents of [[Hydra (Earth-8096)|Hydra]]. During the battle, Iron Man realized that the mechs Hydra was using were actually built with some [[Stark Industries (Earth-8096)|Stark Industries]] components. S.H.I.E.L.D. arrived in the midst of the battle, sending in their own mechs to help out Iron Man. The enemies were all defeated, but when Iron Man realized that the S.H.I.E.L.D. mechs were also composed of Stark Tech, Tony was less than pleased.{{r|Avengers Micro Episodes: Iron Man Season 1 2}} He boarded [[Nicholas Fury (Earth-8096)|Nick Fury]]'s [[S.H.I.E.L.D. Helicarrier|Helicarrier]], demanding an explanation. Nick Fury explained that that was what Stark Industries was supposed to be doing: supplying S.H.I.E.L.D. with weapons.{{r|Avengers Micro Episodes: Iron Man Season 1 3}}

===Founding of the Avengers===
Around the same time of a massive super-villain breakout occurring in four main prisons, Iron Man was on a mission to [[Latveria]] where he dismantled a weapons exchange between [[Advanced Idea Mechanics (Earth-8096)|A.I.M.]] agents and some of [[Victor von Doom (Earth-8096)|Dr. Doom]]'s forces. Upon returning back home he received a transmission from [[Virginia Potts (Earth-8096)|Pepper Potts]], informing him of a massive breakout.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 1}} Tony Stark and several other superheroes soon found themselves thrust into a violent confrontation with [[Franklin Hall (Earth-8096)|Graviton]], a supervillain that Nick Fury had detained in an underwater prison for several years. With the combined efforts of Iron Man, [[Henry Pym (Earth-8096)|Ant-Man]], [[Janet Van Dyne (Earth-8096)|Wasp]], [[Thor Odinson (Earth-8096)|Thor]], and even [[Bruce Banner (Earth-8096)|Hulk]], the superheroes finally managed to subdue the powerful supervillain. Although Tony Stark had preferred to work alone, he came to realize that there were some threats that he couldn't defeat alone. So on that day, Iron Man and the other members of the team officially declared themselves "The Avengers".{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 2}}

[[File:Anthony Stark (Earth-8096) from Avengers Micro Episodes Iron Man Season 1 1 0002.png|thumb|right]]
Early on in the Avengers' history, the [[Amora (Earth-8096)|Enchantress]] used the Hulk to try to fracture and weaken the team. Despite defeating the breaker of worlds, the team was soon ambushed by the Enchantress herself and her [[Skurge (Earth-8096)|Executioner]]. Although the Hulk returned to turn the tide of battle, ultimately the Hulk left the team, upset at the team's distrust.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 3}}

While searching for the Hulk up in the icy north, the team discovered the frozen body of [[Steven Rogers (Earth-8096)|Captain America]]. After Iron Man detected that the war hero was still alive, the Avengers transported him back to the States. As they approached [[New York City|New York]] Captain America awoke, disoriented from the sixty plus years sleep. Suspecting he was captured by Hydra, the old hero proceeded to fight his way off the [[Quinjet]], stopping only upon sight of his and [[James Buchanan Barnes (Earth-8096)|Bucky]]'s memorial statue. After a joint attack by [[Heinrich Zemo (Earth-8096)|Baron Heinrich Zemo]] and "[[Doughboy (Earth-8096)|Dough Boy]]," Captain America joined the Avengers.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 4}}

Tony had become a changed man after putting on the armor. He changed so much so that he bought [[Simon Williams (Earth-8096)|Simon Williams']] company in order to save it from bankruptcy. His act of kindness was misunderstood by Williams as he sought to seek revenge against Stark by teaming up with his brother [[Eric Williams (Earth-8096)|Grim Reaper]] and A.I.M. Simon had undergone an experimental procedure that turned him into living ionic energy and transformed him into Wonder Man. Simon attacked Stark but was stopped by the Avengers just before his ionic energy became unstable and disappearing into nothingness. Tony had regretted not informing Simon of his business decision to save his company and work with him.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 5}} 

=== Expanding the Team ===
After being tested of their capabilities in front of [[Avengers Mansion]], The Avengers were asked by [[T'Challa (Earth-8096)|Prince T'Challa]] of [[Wakanda]] to help him in overthrowing the [[M'Baku (Earth-8096)|Man-Ape]] and taking down the Hydra base that had been set up their by Grim Reaper and [[Ulysses Klaw (Earth-8096)|Ulysses Klaw]]. The Avengers agreed but were attacked by the Wakandan forces at the border that ended up crashing their Quinjet. Tony was left with Ant-Man and the Wasp in taking down the Wakandan forces along with Grim Reaper and Klaw in the [[Vibranium]] Mounds. After Klaw had ended up turning into pure sound, Iron Man was able to trap the [[Sonic Disruptor]] that was keeping Klaw stable. After T'Challa was able to defeat Man-Ape and reclaim the throne, Stark had let him on the team after Janet reminded him that T'Challa was their only way home.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 6}}

While hunting down [[Clinton Barton (Earth-8096)|Hawkeye]] with the Avengers, they were approached by [[Clay Quartermain (Earth-8096)|Clay Quartermain]] to help with an expanding gamma dome created by [[Samuel Sterns (Earth-8096)|The Leader]]. Stark had created gamma-resistant suits to help the team infiltrate the dome. After the team destroyed the dome generator, the Leader had unleashed a second dome in [[Las Vegas]] that had mutated the team into gamma-irradiated monsters. Soon after, Hawkeye, Hulk, and Thor were able to stop the Leader's plan and save the team along with the rest of the citizens who had been affected. After saving the team, Tony asked Hawkeye to joined the team, but he initially refused. It wasn't until Hulk had agreed to rejoin the team under the condition that Hawkeye join, that they both had join the team.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 7}}{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 8}}

Shortly after returning home, Tony was working on modifying [[Just A Really Very Intelligent System (Earth-8096)|J.A.R.V.I.S]] and his suits so he could call any of the three whenever he wanted, but he was attacked the [[Masters of Evil (Earth-8096)|Masters of Evil]] and captured. It wasn't until Hawkeye, Black Panther, and Ant-Man had freed him and the other captured Avengers that they were able to take down the villain team.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 9}} 

Tony and the other Avengers helped Janet, Hank, [[Carol Danvers (Earth-8096)|Carol Danvers]] and [[Mahr Vehl (Earth-8096)|Captain Marvel]] against a [[Sentry 459 (Earth-8096)|Kree Sentry]] that had attacked a observatory S.H.I.E.L.D. base. After the team had thrown everything they had at the machine, Captain Marvel threw the [[Nega-Bombs|Nega Bomb]] that the machine contained into space, but froze while in the cold vacuum of deep space. Tony was able to save him as Thor threw the bomb far beyond any human's reach.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 10}}

When Hawkeye wanted to chase down [[Natasha Romanoff (Earth-8096)|Black Widow]], Stark and S.H.I.E.L.D. were against it stating that they should focus on recapturing the escaped convicts from the "Breakout." He did help Captain America and Black Panther find the location of Hawkeye and [[Barbara Morse (Earth-8096)|Mockingbird]] on Hydra Island.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 11}}

===Attack of Kang the Conqueror===
When the time-traveller [[Nathaniel Richards (Kang) (Earth-TRN937)|Kang]] arrived to kill Captain America, who he believe to be the future cause of the destruction of Earth, Iron Man managed to get to the villain's special throne to defeat him.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 12}} When Kang escaped, Tony pushed himself to the limit to find Kang's space-ship.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 13}} When the Avengers arrived, he managed to hack it and threatened Kang to send it to the future. Wasp alerted Tony this would cause the death of [[Ravonna Renslayer (Earth-TRN937)|Princess Ravonna]], Kang's wife. Kang was finally imprisoned in the special [[Prison 42]], in the [[Negative Zone]], where the villain claimed the presence of Captain America in this time would cause a war.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 14}}

While fighting [[Chen Lu (Earth-8096)|The Radioactive Man]] alongside Thor and Black Panther, the entire world had been engulfed in a blizzard caused by [[Malekith (Earth-8096)|Malekith the Accursed]] using the [[Casket of Ancient Winters]]. While flying to [[Norway]] to stop Malekith, Thor and Tony got into an argument regarding Tony's obsession with technology and Thor's over reliance on magic. Eventually they realized that they should put aside their differences in favor of the greater good. They combined magic and science to destroy Malekith and close the Casket once and for all.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 15}}

===War on Hydra===
When Tony and the rest of the team were watching Hawkeye make a supposedly impossible shot, the training was cut short due to an EMP knocking out the power not only in the mansion but also Tony's suit. Once they opened the front door of the mansion, it was revealed that Black Widow had caused it. She came to inform them Hydra and A.I.M. had been going to war for control of the [[Cosmic Cube]]. The team reluctantly agreed to help and track down [[Wolfgang von Strucker (Earth-8096)|Baron Wolfgang von Strucker]]. Before they could get to him, Iron Man and Wasp were stopped by S.H.I.E.L.D., now led by [[Maria Hill (Earth-8096)|Maria Hill]]. She ordered them to either stand down or be arrested by S.H.I.E.L.D. Luckily, the situation deescalated after Cap had found Strucker and grabbed the Cube at the same time as him, foiling Strucker's plan, but inadvertently bringing back his war friend [[James Buchanan Barnes (Earth-8096)|Bucky Barnes]].{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 16}}

===Ultron===
Iron Man and the rest of the Avengers found the [[Serpent Society (Earth-8096)|Serpent Society]] holding civilians hostage in a subway and Tony jokingly told the Avengers to stand down and give them access to the Quinjet. Before the battle between the two ensued, Hank intervened and tried to appeal to [[Klaus Voorhees (Earth-8096)|King Cobra]]'s more human side, but failed to do so. The battle escalated until Hank used his ant's on the society, causing them to flee. Later, when Thor asked for Tony's help in his attempt to return to Asgard, [[Ultron (Earth-8096)|Ultron-5]] had taken control of the mansion and attempted to destroy the Avengers. Tony later helped the rest of the team against Ultron to little effect, but were saved when Hulk came and tore apart Ultron-5's body. Tony then ordered Hank to destroy every last file relating to Ultron.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 17}}

After Hank finished destroying all the files relating to Ultron, Ultron-5 simply uploaded himself to Ultron-6 and attacked the Avengers using previous Iron Man armors. Hawkeye and Black Panther stayed behind to take down the armors while the rest of the team went to find Ultron attempting to hack into Director Maria Hill's mind to gain access to S.H.I.E.L.D's nuclear launch codes. Tony tried everything he could to stop the warheads from going off, but was nearly too late until Hank came and reprogrammed Ultron to realize that he was part of the problem he was trying to solve. Just before the warheads could explode, Ultron commenced self-shutdown and the world was saved.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 18}}

===Battle in the Nine Realms===
Iron Man fought the [[Arthur Parks (Earth-8096)|Living Laser]] when the Masters of Evil tried to use the [[Norn Stones]] to bring an invasion from [[Asgard]] to Earth.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 19}} When the Norn Stones were destroyed, Tony was sent to the realm [[Nidavellir]], and after helping defeat [[Ulik (Earth-8096)|Ulik]] the [[Rock Trolls|Rock Troll]], [[Eitri (Earth-8096)|Eitri]] the [[Dwarves of Nidavellir|Dwarf]] agreed to help him make a new armor in order to defeat [[Loki Laufeyson (Earth-8096)|Loki]], who had taken [[Odin Borson (Earth-8096)|Odin]]'s power and Thor prisoner.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 20}} While the rest of the Avengers were defeated, Iron Man used his [[Thorbuster Armor (Earth-8096)|new armor]] to battle Loki until his teammates recovered and fought the Asgardian villain. When Giant-Man damaged the magic tree [[Yggdrasill]], Loki's power returned to Odin, who woke up from his sleep and confronted Loki, sending him to a [[Jormungand (Earth-8096)|new punishment]].{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 1 21}}

===Private War of Doctor Doom===
When the Avengers returned to Earth, Tony and Janet visited the [[Fantastic Four (Earth-8096)|Fantastic Four]] and were greeted by [[Susan Storm (Skrull) (Earth-8096)|Invisible Woman]] and [[Reed Richards (Earth-8096)|Reed Richards]]. Tony briefly began using his old [[Iron Man Armor MK III (Earth-8096)|Mark III]] that seemed less than prepared for a fight, but used it to fight Doctor Doom, who had kidnapped Janet and Invisible Woman. The two teams traveled to [[Latveria]] and invaded the private [[Castle Doom (Doomstadt)|castle]] of [[Victor von Doom (Earth-8096)|Doctor Doom]]. Once they retrieved the two kidnapped heroes, Black Panther realized it was best for them to leave and not escalate a battle on foreign soil. Doom eventually figured out that [[Susan Storm (Earth-8096)|Susan Storm]] had been replaced with a [[Deviant Skrulls|Skrull]] impostor.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 1}}

===Return of the Mandarin===
Sometime after returning to Earth, the Avengers battled [[Fin Fang Foom (Earth-8096)|Fin Fang Foom]] and the [[Mandarin (Earth-8096)|Mandarin]] when the two were terrorizing the area of New York around [[Stark Tower]]. Tony was hit with the fiery breath of Fin Fang Foom and recognized the Mandarin from when he first became Iron Man. Tony told the other Avengers that Mandarin enslaved a quarter of China using the [[Mandarin's Rings|Makluan Rings]]. When the Mandarin was using his ring power on the team, Tony was able to absorb the rings' blasts while Janet shrunk and took the rings off of him. After Fin Fang Foom was no longer under his control, he attacked the Mandarin and the two disappeared.{{r|Marvel Universe Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes Vol 1 1}}

===Return to Asgard===
A while after returning to Earth, Tony and Steve (Skrull) returned to Asgard to retrieve whatever was left of the [[Paul Duval (Earth-8096)|Grey Gargoyle]] after they heard that the Masters of Evil had killed and left him there. When they arrived, they witnessed a battle ensuing with Thor, [[Sif (Earth-8096)|Sif]], and the [[Warriors Three (Earth-8096)|Warriors Three]] against Rock Trolls and helped them fight. After then traveling to [[Nornheim]], they found the victims of the Grey Gargoyle and discovered that he was able to reassemble himself after being shattered by Skurge the Executioner. After they all failed to weaken him, Tony put his iron gauntlets onto Duval's hands so that he wouldn't be able to turn anything into stone. They were then able to save the victims of Gery Gargoyle and return [[Karnilla (Earth-8096)|Karnilla]] to her rightful place on the throne of Nornheim with Thor saying he will join the Avengers one day soon.{{r|Marvel Universe Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes Vol 1 2}}

===Alone against A.I.M===
Days later, Tony created a new Iron Man Armor, the [[Iron Man Armor MK IX (Earth-8096)|Mark IX]], which he used to fight A.I.M., when that group tried to steal all Stark's data from the Stark Tower by using [[Technovore (Earth-8096)|Technovore]] to attack all Arc Reactor energy readings. Luckily, during this attack, Panther, Skrull Cap, and [[James Rhodes (Earth-8096)|Colonel James Rhodes]] had been in the building and were able to help hold back the A.I.M goons, especially after Rhodes had donned his [[War Machine Armor (Earth-8096)|War Machine Armor]]. Before the attack, Stark was having a meeting with Director Hill of S.H.I.E.L.D. She had tried to convince him that the Avengers needed to join S.H.I.E.L.D. They were suddenly attacked by Technovore but they were able to escape the data-consuming monster and get Tony's new armor. The team had led Technovore to the room containing the Arc Reactor that powered the entire building and Tony was able to force feed it all the energy until it overloaded and exploded. After the battle, Stark had stuck with his position of not registering and working for S.H.I.E.L.D.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 2}}

===The Return of the Masters of Evil===
While attempting to hunt down the remaining Masters of Evil, Tony and Janet found out that [[Curtis Carr (Earth-8096)|Chemistro]] had been encased in a solid gold shell. When they returned to the mansion, they found Zemo, [[Emil Blonsky (Earth-8096)|Abomination]], Wonder Man asking for their help against Enchantress who had been hunting down former members of the Masters of Evil. The team reluctantly agreed to help, so Stark and Clint traveled to [[Ivan Vanko (Crimson Dynamo) (Earth-8096)|Crimson Dynamo]]'s location and saved him from Amora. When they all returned to the mansion, they had created a device to dampen her magical powers. The plan was going well until Zemo had betrayed the Avengers and ordered Dynamo and Wonder Man to destroy the Avengers. Tony was caught off guard and attacked by Dynamo. The fight between the two teams came to a halt when Simon grabbed the Norn Stone from Enchantress that Zemo had threatened her with and sacrificed himself to destroy it and banish her.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 3}}

===Return of the Kree===
Later when the [[Kree Empire]] returned to Earth, Hulk informed Tony and Cap (still being played by a Skrull) of what was happening. The three met up with [[Carol Danvers (Earth-8096)|Ms. Marvel]] who had also been confronting the Kree at this time. A battle ensued between the Avengers and [[Ronan (Earth-8096)|Ronan the Accuser]]. After the battle, the Kree had surrendered when [[Sentient World Observation and Response Department (Earth-8096)|S.W.O.R.D]] had taken them down and Ronan was imprisoned in Prison 42. After imprisoning Ronan and Captain Marvel, Tony asked Ms. Marvel to join them as an Avenger, which she gladly accepted.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 4}}

===Korvac===
After Wasp took in a homeless man by the name of [[Michael Korvac (Earth-8096)|Michael Korvac]], Stark and the other Avengers came to investigate the mental stability of Korvac. Janet later left to go find Korvac's [[Corrina Walters (Earth-8096)|wife]]. After she came back, the [[Guardians of the Galaxy (Earth-8096)|Guardians of the Galaxy]] came and attacked the Avengers to get to Korvac. Stark battled [[Phyla-Vell (Earth-8096)|Quasar]] in the skies above Avengers Mansion and was initially worried when she used her [[Quantum Bands]] to conjure huge weapons that attacked him. He was able to use his rockets and knock her out, but before she fell to the ground Stark heard her speak English and became suspicious of her origins. After catching her, once she fell in the mansion's pool, the Guardians and Avengers were attacked by Korvac who was driven mad by his powers. Luckily, [[Adam Warlock (Earth-8096)|Warlock]] had saved them all by teleporting them all inside the [[Soul Stone|Soul Gem]]. The Guardians later explained who Korvac was and why he was a danger to the galaxy. The two teams teamed up and surprise-attacked Korvac in [[Central Park]]. Tony tried to convince him to stop so they could help but they realized they were no match for him. Korvac finally disappeared into deep space once his wife told him that he had became a monster.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 6}}

===Skrull Infiltration===
While Tony and the other Avengers were celebrating Ms. Marvel officially joining the team, they noticed [[John Horton (Earth-8096)|Griffin]] attacking the streets of New York and went to go fight him. Tony stayed behind the pay the check but was sedated and kidnapped by Black Widow. He was brought to a secret location where Fury had been with his [[Secret Warriors (Earth-8096)|new team]] he had secretly assembled. It was revealed to Tony that a [[Madame Viper (Skrull) (Earth-8096)|Skrull]] had been impersonating [[Ophelia Sarkissian (Earth-8096)|Madame Hydra]] for over a year and that it was likely someone within the Avengers had also been switched with a Skrull double. After this meeting, Tony returned to the mansion and spied on the team until he accused Hawkeye of being the Skrull. This led to a battle between the sides that defended Hawkeye and those who did not. After everyone had calmed down, the team was in pieces and some (such as Tony, T'Challa, and Carol) left due to the lack of trust. This left Hulk, Hawkeye, Wasp, and "Captain America" as being the only ones on the team.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 7}}

Tony had been working on a device that would detect alien signatures but to no avail when Doom had burst into his workspace and given him a chip to implant in his armor that would allow him see which individuals had been secretly Skrulls. He was later taken by Black Widow to Fury's secret base where Fury and the rest of the Secret Warriors had been stunned and incapacitated by [[Veranke (Earth-8096)|Queen Veranke]] who had been impersonating Mockingbird and revealed that they were able to upload a virus into Tony's suit, incapacitating him as well.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 11}} Stark was later saved by Maria Hill who, with the help of Fury, removed and repaired their arc reactor. He then flew to [[Washington, D.C.]] and used the device he developed to reveal Skrulls true identities on both Queen Veranke and Pitt'o Nili. During the battle between the heroes and [[Super-Skrulls]], Stark was able to tell Thor about the satellites that were targeting human signatures and have him destroy them. Once the Skrulls were taken care of, he gave his technology to [[Sydren (Earth-8096)|Sydren]] and the rest of SWORD so they could track down remaining Skrulls and then taken to [[Prison 42]] until they could figure out what to do with them.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 12}}

Some time after the Skrull Invasion, Tony attempted to clear Cap's name from the libel that was being written about him from [[John Jonah Jameson (Earth-8096)|JJ Jameson]] in the [[Daily Bugle (Earth-8096)|Daily Bugle]] in regards to Cap seemingly selling out Earth to the Skrulls. Jameson only agreed to clear his name if he was to get an interview with Rogers. During the interview, Rogers, [[Elizabeth Brant (Earth-8096)|Betty Brant]] and photographer [[Peter Parker (Earth-8096)|Peter Parker]] were attacked by the [[Serpent Society (Earth-8096)|Serpent Society]] and later Tony, alongside the rest of the Avengers were able to save the heroes and civilians from the collapsing sewer that they had fallen into.{{r|Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes (animated series) Season 2 13}}

