| History                 = Because he attended the premiere of his own movie, ''[[Iron Man 2 (film)|Iron Man 2]]'', Iron Man arrived late to the [[Stark Expo]], where he was supposed to be hosting the "Iron Mania" celebrity trivia quiz show. When he got there, he encountered somebody impersonating. When they came face to face, the impersonator fled with the money the show had raised for charity. The impersonator dropped his helmet taking off, revealing himself as [[Wade Wilson (Earth-93342)|Deadpool]].{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 12}}

Tony later accidentally trapped himself in his own [[Hall of Armor]] during [[Lucas Cage (Earth-93342)|Luke Cage]]'s visit at the Stark Tower.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 13}}

One time during the Holidays, Iron Man was one of the [[Avengers (Earth-93342)|Avengers]] who didn't let [[Peter Parker (Earth-93342)|Spider-Man]] join their team. When [[Heinrich Zemo (Earth-93342)|Baron Zemo]] kidnapped the Avengers, Iron Man sent a distress signal in the form of a [[Spider-Signal]] to the web slinger, who heeded the call and rescued them. Spider-Man became part of the Avengers afterwards.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 16}}

When watching the {{WP|Super Bowl|big game}} at the [[Stark Tower|Avengers Tower]], following the reformation of the team and celebration of the [[Heroic Age (Event)|Heroic Age]], Iron Man and [[Steven Rogers (Earth-93342)|Captain America]] found themselves once again in opposite sides because Tony was a fan of Pittsburgh's team, whereas Steve was a fan of the Football Club from Green Bay. This almost caused a new conflict until Spider-Man distracted them with the commercials. After watching the TV ads, Tony and Steve settled their differences, agreeing that the unity of the Avengers shouldn't be threatened for something as petty as a football game. However, both Tony and Cap reached at the same time for the last nacho in the bowl. With none of them willing to give in, Iron Man and Cap ended up fighting.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 17}}

Tony later hosted the {{WP|83rd Academy Awards|83rd Annual Movie Film Awards}}. When he was going to announce the winner for the category "Best Picture," [[George Tarleton (Earth-93342)|M.O.D.O.K.]], [[Wade Wilson (Earth-93342)|Deadpool]], and [[Aleksandr Topolov (Earth-93342)|Gremlin]] crashed the event to present their own nominees. After numerous attempts, Tony finally managed to dismiss the intruders, and reveal the movie ''Quack to the Future'' as the winner.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 18}}

When Ultron returned to destroy the Avengers, Iron Man was one of the heroes who tried to stop the evil android. However, Ultron received a software update message, for which the Avengers waited until he finished downloading it. Several hours later, Ultron's download finished, but when he was finally ready to destroy the Avengers, his systems required to be rebooted.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 26}}

After some time of growing apart from his best friend [[James Rhodes (Earth-93342)|War Machine]] since getting his [[Iron Man Armor Model 37|new armor]], Tony planned to go to [[Las Vegas]], and asked Rhodey to take his place guarding the Earth for the time of his trip. Enraged by Tony's mistreatment, Rhodey called him out and left him to get a new partner. Tony eventually reached out to Rhodey, who was now going by the name of [[Iron Patriot]], and apologized. After asking if the next step of their reconciliation was to become an Avenger, Tony told him that they'd best try to be best friends for the time being.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 27}}

Iron Man later attended the Avengers Tower Halloween Party, dressed as {{WP|Han Solo}}.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 37}}

Not wanting to pay for cable, [[Stephen Strange (Earth-93342)|Doctor Strange]] opened a portal for him to view other universes, eventually he found [[Earth-616|the prime universe]] and began to binge watch. He then forced others to view this universe, including Iron Man, who saw that that universe he could remove his armor. [[Thanos (Earth-93342)|Thanos]] obtained the [[Infinity Gauntlet]] to widen the portals to allow Iron Man and others to pass through. Arriving in a 2-D world, the Infinity Gauntlet blew away. At this point Doctor Strange had gotten bored and eradicated the universe they were in, transporting everyone back to the correct universe.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 50}}

[[Scott Lang (Earth-93342)|Ant-Man]] was called to the [[Avengers (Earth-93342)|Avengers]] 4th July picnic because they thought he was an exterminator, which Iron Man was present for. After removing the ants with his [[Ant-Man's Helmet|helmet]] he tried to convince them he was a super hero by growing and shrinking, however nothing would convince them, [[Clinton Barton (Earth-93342)|Hawkeye]] even left a review for his non existent exterminator service.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 51}}

After being unfrozen decades, Captain America began to miss his allies from his own decade. At some point Dum Dum Dugan was a [[Life Model Decoy]] of the [[Timothy Dugan (Earth-93342)|original]], who was presented to Captain America by Iron Man.{{r|Marvel Super Heroes: What The--?! Season 1 53}}

